// Canonical source: a property word stands as a member's name where the
// grammar can tell it is one: after the member's type, before '(' ';' '=' or
// '['. A property word is an attribute only inside [ ] (thesis line 640).
// hidden (line 688) and shared (line 665) here name a field and a method.
// Answer: 12 (5 + 7).
class P : Object { section [public] { int hidden; int shared() { return 7; } P() { this.hidden = 5; } } }
P p = new P();
return p.hidden + p.shared();
